    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution input into F, the dense feature field that carries spatial information. The window operator then partitions that field into X for processing. The equation keeps every token by applying windowing to the feature field rather than replacing it with a compact vector.",
